# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm pending metadata command storage is a single entry per `(PG,bucket)` and overwrites via `HashMap::insert`.
- [x] Confirm overwrite protection is only `debug_assert!`, so optimized/release builds do not enforce it.
- [x] Confirm the stream `CreateStreamUpload` paths added by the commit call `set_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket` after drain/reservation and depend on this shared slot.
- [x] Confirm partial metadata apply intentionally leaves commands pending for retry, so losing the slot loses retry state.
- [x] Dynamically demonstrate debug collision crash and release silent overwrite of a first `CreateStreamUpload` pending command by a second command with the same `(PG,bucket)`.
## Report
Validated the core finding. Code review showed the pending-command slot is keyed only by (PgId, BucketName) and `set_pending_metadata_command_for_bucket` performs `HashMap::insert` followed only by `debug_assert!(previous.is_none())` at `crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:270-284`; therefore release builds silently overwrite an existing pending command. The new stream-create paths publish `CreateStreamUpload` commands into that slot at `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:1611-1627` and `crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:3307-3344` after a drain/check/reservation sequence, so a concurrent operation that has already passed its drain can later publish another command for the same bucket/PG. Partial apply retry semantics depend on the pending command remaining present: `apply_pending_object_metadata_command_for_bucket` removes only on success at `crates/storage/src/cluster.rs:885-901`, and `apply_new_object_metadata_command_for_bucket` removes on error only when `applied_nodes == 0` at `crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:2119-2128`. I added a focused unit PoC that inserts two `CreateStreamUpload` commands for the same `(PG,bucket)`. In debug, it crashes exactly at the debug assertion, proving the collision is reachable. In release, the same PoC succeeds and prints `PoC overwrite: first_log_index=1 stored_log_index=2 command_a_lost=true`, proving the first pending retry state is silently discarded. I also ran the existing `stream_put_create_partial_apply_retry_reuses_existing_session` test, which passed and confirms the intended invariant that a partially applied stream create remains pending for retry. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable; LLDB was used non-interactively to run the release PoC and observed the same overwrite behavior with process exit 0.

